uline,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"schanze":{"entries":[["schanze",null,"/ˈʃantsə/","Of uncertain origin. Attested since the 15th century. Several etymologies have been proposed.\nPfeifer suggests the regional Franconian/Hessian term Schanze (“basket”) (itself of unknown origin) as the origin, arguing that entrenchments resemble baskets from the inside, being dug-out earth pits that have been reinforced from the inside with brushwood. He rejects a derivation from Italian scansi (noun), plural of scanso, claiming that such theories are based on an unverifiable meaning of “defense”/“resistance” of the Italian term.\nSee also Dutch schans, Danish skanse, Swedish skans and English sconce.",{"g":"f","decl":"||||n|n|n|n"}]],"senses":[[11575,"schanze","noun","entrenchment, redoubt",0,"f"],[11576,"schanze","noun","ramp; jump (an installation, either temporary or permanent, that is driven over quickly (with skis, a bike etc.) so that the driver is propelled into the air)",1,"f"],[11577,"schanze","name","ellipsis of Sternschanze, an area of Hamburg, Germany",2,null,["colloquial"]]]},"topasen":{"entries":[["topasen",null,null,"Topas + -en"]],"senses":[[45869,"topasen","adj","topaz",0,null,["rare"]],[45870,"topasen","noun","dative plural of Topas",1,"m"]],"inflections":[["topasen","topas","dative,definite,plural"]]},"träfet":{"entries":[["träfet",null,null,null]],"senses":[[104880,"träfet","verb","second-person plural subjunctive II of treffen",0]],"inflections":[["träfet","treffen","formal,plural,rare,second-person,subjunctive,subjunctive-ii"]]},"wanderfalke":{"entries":[["wanderfalke",null,"/ˈvandərfalkə/","From wandern + Falke.",{"g":"m","decl":"|n|n|n|n|n|n|n"}]],"senses":[[34977,"wanderfalke","noun","peregrine falcon, Falco peregrinus",0,"m"]]},"weidetet aus":{"entries":[["weidetet aus",null,null,null]],"senses":[[391482,"weidetet aus","verb","inflection of ausweiden:",0],[391483,"weidetet aus","verb","second-person plural preterite",1],[391484,"weidetet aus","verb